ResponseConfigInput.description:
The response a custom session answers every webhook with. Every violation is `400` / `1005 INVALID_RESPONSE_CONFIG`.

Limits JSON Schema cannot express, because they count **bytes of the UTF-8 encoding** (1 KiB = 1024 bytes):
- `body` at most 65536 bytes (64 KiB) and must not contain U+0000; any text is accepted, JSON or not;
- the header block — the sum of `name: value\r\n` over the configured pairs only — at most 8192 bytes (8 KiB);
- a status of `204`, `205` or `304` with a non-empty `body` is rejected;
- with `template: true`, a `body` holding a `{{` that does not start one of the placeholders `template` lists, closed by `}}` with nothing else inside the braces, is rejected; the message names the placeholder by its place and quotes none of it;
- a `Location` header is rejected unless `status` is from 300 to 399 and its value begins with the literal `/s/`, a path on the webhook host such as `/s/<sessionId>/after`.

Reserved header names, rejected case-insensitively: `Content-Length`, `Content-Encoding`, `X-Content-Type-Options`, `Transfer-Encoding`, `Connection`, `Keep-Alive`, `Upgrade`, `TE`, `Trailer`, `Host`, `Set-Cookie`, `Refresh`, `Alt-Svc`, `WWW-Authenticate`, `Proxy-Authenticate`, `Clear-Site-Data`, `Strict-Transport-Security`, `Content-Security-Policy`, `Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only`, `Public-Key-Pins`, `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials`, `NEL`, `Report-To`, `Reporting-Endpoints`, `X-Webhook-Inspector-Request-Id`, and any name beginning with `X-QA-Tools-`. Every other name is allowed, `Location` apart, as above, duplicates included — `Content-Type` among them, sent as configured.
